# Q: is the ground a map file shaped, and does the battle stand on it?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --map-file maps/demo-isthmus.map.json --probe tools/probe/map-file.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/map-file.txt
#
# The format §10 describes, applied: the height edits lower the map's centre into a basin and
# paint the ore on its floor, the derived passes are re-run from the edited ground — the bands,
# the fords, the connectivity — and the mission is laid out on the land that now exists. The
# loader has already refused what the placement rules refuse, so what is read here is the
# shaped ground itself.
#
#   - `surfaces` is the census of what the edits made: the ore is where the author painted it,
#     and the basin reads as what it now is.
#   - `attributes` on the painted cells says the same thing per cell, in the words the ground
#     itself uses.
#   - `validate` sits the authored mission under the same check the campaign sits under.

validate
surfaces
attributes 30 30
attributes 31 31
tick 120
